WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.230
On the coast of North Antrim stand
over 40,000 columns of basalt:

2
00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.110
the Giant's Causeway.

3
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.390
It was inscribed as a World
Heritage Site in 1986.

4
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.810
Most of it is owned and
managed by the National Trust.

5
00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:20.650
In 2012, a new visitor centre opened,
clad in basalt to fit the landscape.

6
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:25.290
A million visitors a year come to
this one small stretch of coast.

7
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.130
Is that regeneration, or a problem?

8
00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:31.430
In this mission, you'll sort
the strategies used here,

9
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:35.830
from heritage tourism to kayak
trails and farm diversification.

10
00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.910
Then you'll line up everyone
with a stake in this coast,

11
00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.490
from conservation bodies to residents.

12
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:46.710
Your mission: evaluate whether tourism
on the Causeway Coast is regeneration or

13
00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:47.570
a problem.
